 "description": "Kestrel Plains Health and Community Care Network is an invented public health service in a regional Australian setting. It runs two acute hospitals, a district hospital, an urgent care centre, community health centres, a bush nursing centre, residential aged-care homes and adult and youth mental-health services across a wide inland catchment. Its services include inpatient and outpatient care, hospital-in-the-home, community nursing, allied health, palliative care, maternal and child health, home support for older people and community mental-health outreach. A Board governs the network through a Chief Executive Officer, an executive team and a set of clinical governance, consumer, staff and advisory committees. Every name, number and identifier in this profile is fictional and institutional.",
